n loopback health tokens without opening a socket.\n\n## Approach\n\nParse the shipped final Docker stage and inspect its effective entrypoint, installed artifacts, and health command. Execute the configured health command against controlled good and bad listeners so the oracle observes a real socket and response. Keep this in the portable Python test path; do not require Docker.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp`\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot`\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd a broken trailing-stage fixture, a no-op URL-print command, a healthy listener, and malformed/closed-listener controls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A broken shipped final stage fails even when an earlier stage retains all expected tokens.\n- [ ] A command that only prints the health URL fails the oracle.\n- [ ] The real configured health command succeeds against a valid listener and fails on closed or malformed response paths.\n- [ ] The focused tests run without Docker and leave normal local/default test dependencies unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py","reason":"parse final-stage semantics and execute MCP health command"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"replace token-only review-bot health assertion with behavior"},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp","reason":"shipped MCP stage under semantic contract"},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot","reason":"shipped review-bot stage under semantic contract"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"authoritative health command and service wiring"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"